  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="6">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IIIEm">III Em</ref> 6</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="6" corresp="#wit-q">Et dictum est de uestigatione et quesitione pecoris furati, ut ad uillam peruestigetur, et non sit foristeallum aliquod illi uel aliqua prohibitio itineris uel questionis.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="la" source="#robertson" n="6" corresp="#wit-q">Et dictum est de investigatione et quaesitione [pecoris furati], ut ad villam pervestigetur, et non sit foristeallum aliquod illi vel aliqua prohibitio itineris vel quaestionis.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-q">And we have declared with regard to the tracking and pursuit of stolen cattle, that thorough investigation shall be made at the village, and that no obstacle shall be placed in the way thereof or anything to prevent the pursuit and search.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="191"><ref target="clause:IIEw_4">II Ew 4</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">Vgl. II Ew. 4</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="378"><ref target="clause:Hu_Inscr">Hu</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="344"><ref target="clause:VAtr_29">V Atr 29</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="344"><ref target="clause:VAtr_31">V Atr 31–31.1</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="344"><ref target="clause:VIAtr_36">VI Atr 36</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">Latin only; no German translation in Liebermann. Liebermann compares II Ew 4.</note>
      </div>
